#   4. CLI inbox list              -> crates/famp/src/cli/inbox/list.rs:72
#   5. CLI await                   -> crates/famp/src/cli/await_cmd/mod.rs:137,156,203,227,362
#                                      (156 is write_outcome's own definition —
#                                      the shared helper anchor, not a second
#                                      implementation)
#   6. CLI register --tail         -> crates/famp/src/cli/register.rs:211,288,353,376
#                                      (353 is emit_tail_line's own definition —
#                                      same helper-anchor note as above)
#   7. CLI wait-reply              -> crates/famp/src/cli/wait_reply.rs:35
#                                      (shares write_outcome with #5)
#
# Non-rendering hits carried with justification (verified NOT an eighth
# surface — each is safe either because it emits no received-content text
# to any output a human or downstream consumer reads, or because the
# content it does emit was already wrapped and origin-tagged by an
# upstream render step before this site ever sees it):
#
# justification: crates/famp/src/cli/await_cmd/poll.rs:88 (`find_match`) is
#   confirmed dead code — zero call sites anywhere in the tree (grepped
#   2026-07-31; also documented in 14-02-SUMMARY.md's key-decisions: "the
#   real live path is famp::cli::await_cmd::run_at_structured's AwaitOk
#   arm ... poll.rs was left untouched"). It matches the `envelope-body`
#   family only because `EnvelopeView` is in scope in this file. Not
#   routed through render_envelope_body because it is unreachable, not
#   because it is exempt from the rule — if it is ever wired up, route it
#   through the shared helper first and remove this justification.
# justification: crates/famp-bus/src/broker/handle/tests.rs (8 records,
#   QUAR-07 F2/reply-debug family) — every hit is a `BusReply` bound in a
#   `panic!("expected ..., got {other:?}")` test-assertion arm inside
#   `crates/famp-bus/src/broker/handle/tests.rs`. That file is included
#   only via a `#[cfg(test)] mod tests;` declaration in the sibling
#   `mod.rs`; the `#[cfg(test)]` annotation lives in the parent file, not
#   in `tests.rs` itself, so this script's single-file `strip_noise` brace
#   tracker cannot see the boundary and treats the whole file as
#   production source. It is not: none of these panics ever compile into
#   a non-test binary, and a `panic!` message is observed only by the
#   `cargo test` harness, never by a production error string, stderr
#   line, or MCP tool result. `famp-bus` is one of the six crates frozen
#   for the whole v1.1 milestone (byte-identical pre/post this plan), so
#   restructuring the file to give the mechanical query file-local
#   visibility into the `#[cfg(test)]` boundary is out of scope here — if
#   `famp-bus` is ever unfrozen, split `tests.rs` so it carries its own
#   `#[cfg(test)]` line, or teach `strip_noise` to look at the includer,
#   and remove this justification.
#
